= Вывод @eq-nls-2

The equation @eq-nls-2 derivation is pretty straightforward#footnote[Текст оставлен на английском, но он понятен и так.].
First, from #cite(<gentle2017matrix>) #cite(<magnus2019matrix>) we know, that
$
  dif f= tr [ (frac(d f, d A))' dif A ] \
  dif f= dif (tr f) = tr (dif f)
$
where $tr$ is the trace function, i.e. the sum of the diagonal elements of a matrix, $A$ is a matrix, $f$ is a scalar function.
We have
$ f = sum^T_(t = 1) (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) $

Using the following properties of differential and trace
$
  dif A= (dif a_(i j)) \
  dif (A B) = dif A thin B + A thin dif B \
  dif tr A = tr (dif A) \
  dif A'= (dif A)' \
  tr A= tr A' \
  tr (A B) = tr (B A)) \
  tr (A + B) = tr A + tr B
$
we get the following chain of expressions
$
  dif f & = tr (dif sum^T_(t = 1) (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)) = \
  & = tr sum^T_(t = 1) dif [ (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) ] = \
  & = sum^T_(t = 1) tr dif [ (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) ] = \
  & = sum^T_(t = 1) tr [ dif (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) + (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' dif (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) ] = \
  & = - sum^T_(t = 1) tr [ dif (Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) + (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' dif (Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) ] = \
  & = - sum^T_(t = 1) { tr [ dif (Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) ] + tr [ (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' dif (Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) ] } = \
  & = - sum^T_(t = 1) { tr [ (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' dif (Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) ] + tr [ (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' dif (Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) ] } = \
  & = - 2 tr [ sum^T_(t = 1) (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' dif (Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) ] = bigast
$
Here we use $bigast$ to mark the break in the expression chain.
To proceed, let's simplify the differential inside the sum
$
  dif (Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) & = dif Vect(Psi'_(t)) (Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) + Vect(Psi)'_(t)dif (Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) = \
  & = Vect(Psi)'_(t)(dif Vect(B)' Vect(x)_t + Vect(B)'dif Vect(x)_t) = \
  & = Vect(Psi)'_(t)dif Vect(B)' thin Vect(x)_(t).
$
For every $t$ we can consider $Vect(Psi)_t$ and $Vect(x)_t$ as constants, hence their differentials are zero. With that, we get
$
  bigast& = - 2 tr [ sum^T_(t = 1) (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' Vect(Psi)'_(t)dif Vect(B)' Vect(x)_t ] = \
  & = - 2 tr [ sum^T_(t = 1) Vect(x)'_(t)dif Vect(B)_t med Vect(Psi)_t (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) ] = bigast
$

From $tr (A B) = tr (B A)$ it follows that $tr (A_1 A_2 dots A_n) = tr (A_n A_1 dots A_(n - 1))$.
Then we have
$
  bigast& = - 2 tr [ sum^T_(t = 1) Vect(Psi)_t (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) Vect(x)'_(t)dif Vect(B) ] = \
  & = tr { [ - 2 sum^T_(t = 1) Vect(Psi)_t (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) Vect(x)'_(t) ] dif Vect(B) } .
$

Hence, we get
$
  frac(d f, d Vect(B)) = [ - 2 sum^T_(t = 1) Vect(Psi)_t (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t) Vect(x)'_(t) ]' = - 2 sum^T_(t = 1) Vect(x)_t (Vect(y)_t - Vect(Psi)'_(t)Vect(B)'Vect(x)_t)' Vect(Psi)'_(t)
$

= Вывод @eq-nls-3

Let's go back to
$
  op("vec") hat(Vect(B)) = [ T^(- 1) sum^T_(t = 1) (Vect(Psi)_t Vect(Psi)'_(t)) times.o(Vect(x)_t Vect(x)'_(t)) ]^(- 1) [ T^(- 1) sum^T_(t = 1) op("vec") (Vect(x)_t Vect(y)'_(t)Vect(Psi)'_(t)) ] = bigast
$
From #cite(<gentle2017matrix>) we can get the following properties of Kronecker product
$
  (A times.o B)' = A' times.o B' \
  (A times.o B) (C times.o D) = (A C) times.o (B D) \
  op("vec") (A B C) = (C' times.o A) op("vec") B
$
The corresponding matrix products should exist.
Then we have
$
  bigast= [ T^(- 1) sum^T_(t = 1) (Vect(Psi)_t times.o Vect(x)_t) (Vect(Psi)'_(t)times.o Vect(x)'_(t)) ]^(- 1) [ T^(- 1) sum^T_(t = 1) (Vect(Psi)_t times.o Vect(x)_t) op("vec") Vect(x)'_(t) ] = bigast
$

As $Vect(y)_t$ is already a vector then $op("vec") Vect(y)'_(t)= op("vec") Vect(y)_t$.
Hence we have
$
  bigast& = [ sum^T_(t = 1) (Vect(Psi)_t times.o Vect(x)_t) (Vect(Psi)'_(t)times.o Vect(x)'_(t)) ]^(- 1) [ sum^T_(t = 1) (Vect(Psi)_t times.o Vect(x)_t) op("vec") Vect(y)_t ] = \
  & = [ sum^T_(t = 1) Upsilon_t Upsilon'_(t) ]^(- 1) [ sum^T_(t = 1) Upsilon_t op("vec") Vect(y)_t ]
$

Setting $M = (Upsilon_1,Upsilon_2,...,Upsilon_T)'$ we can see that
$ sum^T_(t = 1) Upsilon_t Upsilon'_(t)= M' M $

Setting $Vect(Y) = (Vect(y)'_(1),..., Vect(y)'_(T))'$ we can get
$ sum^T_(t = 1) Upsilon_t op("vec") Vect(y)_t = M' op("vec") (Vect(Y)') $

Hence, we get @eq-nls-3.
In the package#footnote[Данный текст взят из виньетки пакета, который лектор писал для своих нужд при написании своей диссертации.
  Лектору хотелось разобраться в формулах из статьи #cite(<terasvirta2014specification>).
  На сегодняшний день этот пакет уже не нужен, так как в феврале 2024 был опубликован более адекватно написанный пакет...]
the matrix $M$ is built in more vectorized form to avoid loops as much as possible.
The matrix $M$ is defined as follows
$ M= [ mat(
    delim: "(", 1, g_1 (s_1), ..., g_(m - 1) (s_1);
    dots.v, dots.v, , dots.v;
    1, g_1 (s_T), ..., g_(m - 1) (s_T)
  ) times.o I_k times.o e'_(k p + q) ] dot.o [ e'_(k m)times.o Vect(X) times.o e_k ] $ where $g_k (s) = g(s vert gamma_k,c_k)$, $e_N = autolr(underbrace(#[$1,...,1$], N))'$.
$dot.o$ denotes Hadamard (element-wize) product.
